} } \right] 

 {A^4} = \left[ {\matrix{ {{x^2} + 1} & x  \cr x & 1  \cr

} } \right]\left[ {\matrix{ {{x^2} + 1} & x  \cr x & 1  \cr

} } \right] 

 = \left[ {\matrix{ {{{({x^2} + 1)}^2} + {x^2}} & {x({x^2} + 1) + x}  \cr {x({x^2} + 1) + x} & {{x^2} + 1}  \cr

} } \right] 

Given ${({x^2} + 1)^2} + {x^2} = 109$

Let ${x^2} + 1$ = t

${t^2} + t - 1 = 109 \Rightarrow$ (t  -  10) (t + 11) = 0

$\therefore$ t = 10 = $x^{2}$ + 1 = $a_{22}$

